    "result_text": "I've added both helpers to `hc/front/views.py`, and I'm wrapping up the pattern check. I haven't run the Django tests or the existing call sites.\n\n- **`_get_check_for_user(request, code, preload_owner_profile=False)`** returns `(check, rw)`. Superusers and the project owner get `rw=True`. Anyone else must be a project member, otherwise it returns a 404. A member gets `rw` from their membership.\n- **`_get_rw_check_for_user(request, code)`** returns the check, or raises `PermissionDenied` for read-only members.\n\nThe existing call sites already use `preload_owner_profile=True`, so I added that parameter. When it's set, the query pulls in `project__owner__profile`, which the pattern doesn't have. Otherwise the code follows the `access.channel_for_user@v1` pattern, with the `# pcat:` marker above each function.\n\nMy first `check_code` run reported 5 high-severity deviations. That run had no imports, so it couldn't see `get_object_or_404` or `PermissionDenied`. I re-ran it with the imports and got no high-severity deviations. The two that remain are the extra parameter (medium) and the extra `if` branch (low), and both come from the request, so no `pcat-allow` line is needed."
